{
  "requirement": "Distinguishes a domain operation failure, a missing agent, a provider connection or request failure, an agent protocol failure, and an error encoding or decoding the output.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub enum ValidationError<E> {\n    Graph(E),\n    NoAgentConfigured,\n    Agent(String),\n    Provider(std::io::Error),\n    Output(serde_json::Error),\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<E: Debug> Debug for ValidationError<E>;\nimpl<E: Display> Display for ValidationError<E>;\nimpl<E: Error + 'static> Error for ValidationError<E>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject text asks for two things. The first is that `ValidationError<E>` has five distinct variants: `Graph`, `NoAgentConfigured`, `Agent(String)`, `Provider(io::Error)` and `Output(serde_json::Error)`. The second is that it implements `Debug`, `Display` and `Error`. The text fixes no message formats and no `source` behaviour beyond that, so I did not require tests for them. I judged the tests from the supplied source and did not request any implementation source.\n\nCoverage by variant:\n- **`Graph(E)`:** `tests/contracts.rs#fn[refresh_propagates_load_decode_check_execution_and_save_errors]` matches `ValidationError::Graph(actual)` and asserts the domain error for the load, read, edges, execute and store stages. `agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload` in `graph/validation_tests.rs` checks that `Graph(io::Error)` exposes its inner error through `source()`.\n- **`NoAgentConfigured`:** `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` asserts that a verify with no agent returns exactly `Err(NoAgentConfigured)`. It also asserts that nothing is stored or read.\n- **`Agent(String)`:**\n  - `invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error` asserts `Agent(_)` for an invalid typed submission.\n  - `assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results` asserts `Agent(error)` with the protocol-failure message when the model returns only text.\n  - `agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload` asserts the `String` payload, `Display` as `agent: provider detail`, and `source()` returning `None`.\n- **`Provider(io::Error)`:**\n  - `assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results` asserts `Provider(error)` containing `permanent provider failure`.\n  - `agent/configured.rs#fn[configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors]` asserts `Provider(_)` with a `Display` string that contains the missing credential name.\n  - These tests also keep `Provider` distinct from `Agent`, `Graph` and `NoAgentConfigured`.\n- **`Output(serde_json::Error)`:**\n  - The refresh test asserts `Output` for decode failures on current, stale and unversioned records.\n  - `refresh_serialization_failure_preserves_the_saved_record` and `serialization_failure_leaves_the_existing_record_unchanged` assert `Output` for an encode failure. The second also checks the `Display` text and that the saved record is unchanged.\n\nCoverage by trait:\n- **`Debug`:** the refresh test's fallback arm formats the error with `{other:?}`, which also needs the `E: Debug` bound.\n- **`Display`:** `to_string()` is asserted for `Agent`, `Provider` and `Output`.\n- **`Error`:** `source()` is asserted for `Agent` and `Graph`.\n\nI found no obligation in the text that goes unchecked, and no requirement-violating behaviour the reviewed tests would accept.",
